    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0294" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1756</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Arthur Reynold
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department acknowledges the receipt of
                    your telegram of March 14, 1917, requesting that the American Minister at Peking
                    endeavor to secure an extension of the time which your representative may be
                    permitted to make investigations in China and conduct negotiations for a loan to
                    the Chinese Government by your bank.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to advise you that the Chinese Minister has just informed the
                    Department that he telegraphed yesterday to Mr. J. J. Abbott, now en route to
                    Peking, that the extension had been granted.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
